  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amentum Services has $2.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company has 428 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $6.2M, and obligations are down 24.4% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $1.7B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $749M and the General Services Administration at $101M. Top markets include Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $944M, Security Guards and Patrol Services at $507M, and Engineering Services at $337M. Historical fiscal-year obligations show FY21 at $1.4B, FY22 at $1.6B, FY23 at $2.5B, FY24 at $3.8B, and FY25 at $3.5B. Computer Facilities Management Services and Aircraft Manufacturing contribute meaningful shares at $125M and $95.4M respectively. This profile focuses on current-year obligations and the industries and agencies that account for most of the activity, presenting a numbers-first view of Amentum Services’ federal business through FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Amentum Services' FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads with $1.7B of FY2026 to date obligations. The Department of Homeland Security and the General Services Administration account for $749M and $101M respectively, so a few agencies drive most obligations. The top markets and top agencies together explain a large portion of the $2.7B total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Amentum Services' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is the largest market at $944M. Security Guards and Patrol Services are $507M and Engineering Services are $337M, with Facilities Support Services at $243M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $125M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Amentum Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Amentum Services has $2.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company has 428 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $6.2M, and obligations are down 24.4% year over year. Annual obligations were FY21 $1.4B, FY22 $1.6B, FY23 $2.5B, FY24 $3.8B, and FY25 $3.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Amentum Services?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys the most from Amentum Services, totaling $1.7B in FY2026 to date. Other top buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $749M, the General Services Administration at $101M, the Department of the Treasury at $87.3M, and the Department of State at $46.4M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Amentum Services sell to the government?",
      "a": "Amentum Services sells services focused on air transportation support and security and technical services, led by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $944M and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $507M. Engineering Services account for $337M, Facilities Support Services account for $243M, and Computer Facilities Management Services account for $125M."
